SUMMARY:Celebrate Abilities Free Concert
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the inaugural performance of the ‘Celebrate Abilities’ Concert Series\, in honor of Disability Pride Month. \nThis all-ages\, inclusive musical performance will feature award-winning singer-songwriter Halley Elwell and The Unsinkables\, Schreiber’s modern band and beautiful artwork from the artists of ASPIE. \nHalley Elwell is a singer-songwriter whose evocative music blends elements of jazz\, folk\, pop\, and rock. Known for her rich voice and insightful lyrics\, Elwell’s music has been featured on radio and television and in apps and has been recognized by ASCAP and the John Lennon Songwriting Contest. In 2025\, she undertook her biggest project yet\, a memoir-style concept album and podcast called Spontaneous Mutation. \nBased on her experiences living with neurofibromatosis\, the project explores chronic illness\, the facial difference movement\, disability\, and the importance of telling new stories about all of them. Elwell is a member of Recording Artists and Music Professionals with Disabilities (RAMPD). Click here to learn more about the concert series.
URL:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/celebrate-abilities-concert/
LOCATION:Saint James Episcopal Church\, 103 North Duke Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
GEO:40.040058;-76.30344
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Saint James Episcopal Church 103 North Duke Street Lancaster PA 17602 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=103 North Duke Street:geo:-76.30344,40.040058
END:VEVENT
